# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the ctest runs of an ASan build (the linux-san
# test preset points LSAN_OPTIONS at this file; ADR-0013). Only allocations a
# third-party library keeps for the life of the process belong here, never a
# leak in our own code: fix that instead. Every entry says why it is here,
# above it.
#
# Format: https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/AddressSanitizerLeakSanitizer#suppressions

# GLFW's X11 platform, from glfwInit: XrmInitialize (in _glfwConnectX11) builds
# Xlib's resource-manager tables and XSupportsLocale (in _glfwInitX11) loads its
# locale database, both kept for the process with no call that frees them.
# glfwTerminate unloads libX11, which held the only pointers to them, so
# LeakSanitizer reports them as leaked, from frames it can no longer name. A
# suppression matches any frame of a leak's stack, and only GLFW's X11 setup has
# these two.
leak:_glfwConnectX11
leak:_glfwInitX11
